# Verification checklist (author completes before any release)

Initial and date each line in your own copy. `reproflow gate check .`
checks the mechanical items below (draft stamps, unresolved verify-tags,
placeholders, secrets); the rest are yours.

## Reproduce
- [ ] Fresh fetch via `code/01_fetch.py`; row counts match PROVENANCE.txt or drift is explained
- [ ] Full pipeline re-run; outputs diff clean against the committed versions
- [ ] Every number in any document re-derived from `stats.json` after the re-run
- [ ] `pytest -q` passes

## Source-level checks
- [ ] Five records checked by hand against the original source pages
- [ ] Source vintages confirmed current
- [ ] Licenses and terms of every source re-read; nothing forbids redistribution

## Before it goes public
- [ ] README, limitations, and any manuscript rewritten in your own voice
- [ ] Draft stamps removed (`04_figures.py --final`); `reproflow gate check .` passes
- [ ] License files, name, ORCID, contact in place
- [ ] Evidence log row written the day of release
